 @Hardwareunboxed  So you delete my comment asking you to make an updated video. Nice. I bet its because I pointed out that your card was the newest release and, ergo with the latest bios. Or you're just not happy with Asus.
Not everyone has this heat issue. It was obviously batch based. 
But just delete all my comments If you dont want meaningful conversations with your viewers

 @boingkster  The heatsink costs, rgb, pcb, higher quality VRMs. Do YOURSELF a favor, and lookup buildzoids breakdown of this card (if you can keep up with his explanations) before talking down this product. 

There are youtubers who plug stuff in, and give a review. 
And then theres youtubers who know wtf the stuff actually does, and break it down, and show its strengths and weaknesses.

 @zero.zero.one.001  Yes I definitely understand it. Really bad customer service as well. Asus seems to be screwing up a lot since a while. First of all the need for many to fix their premium card themselves and now hearing that the customer service treated it like it was nothing?!? I guess I was reasonable lucky with at least not having the fan problem, which itself shows that something is wrong and seems to be an obvious RMA case...
To be honest this is my first Asus card. I Bought it because it is the "perfect" card for my build. Pirate build with a lot, but still subtle (A-)RGB lighting in it. And because the price was great at that moment. It's an Arez instead of a ROG from the short NVidia debacle and almost half the price probably because Arez sounds less popular then ROG to people that just don't know it's the same card except for the name... It's even the "fixed" version, but they managed to put the thermal pad on it like a banana.
But in short I'd feel the same way, did the latest bios solve anything? Guess not, you seem to know your tech. Your card is definitely not okay and they should fix it. Hell with those issues give you an 5700XT!

 @Felix-j3d4b  The Morpheus is great, I have one on the 1080Ti that's in the rig I'm using to write this. I put Noctua NF-A12x25's on it, and set the fan speed to a fixed 40% 
I've never seen the GPU temp go above 67C while gaming, and I can just barely tell if the computer is on or off based on sound.
But yeah, I don't know how the Morpheus would work on Navi.
